+# Research Findings (first pass)
+
+> Answers to the questions on the [Research Agenda](Research-Agenda), keyed by question number. Researched 2026-11-19.
+>
+> **How far to trust this page:** these findings come from web-search result excerpts. **No source below was read in full**, and the Dutch SLO PDFs could not be opened at all (network access blocked), so the SLO figures come from search snippets of those documents. Treat every row as a lead to confirm in the original, not a verified fact.
+>
+> **Status key:** 🟢 a useful answer or strong lead found · 🟡 partial / mixed evidence · ⚪ nothing found yet (needs your own data or a targeted search)
+
+The agenda has **64 questions** (12 + 10 + 11 + 11 + 5 + 6 + 5 + 4), not 80 as first estimated.
+
+---
+
+## 4.1 The Dutch CEFR ranges (the main finding)
+
+**Short answer: official end-of-programme targets exist, but the per-year table in the app does not appear to come from a government source, and some of its end-point cells look higher than the official targets.**
+
+What the SLO (national curriculum institute) sources say, from search excerpts:
+
+| School type | Official target (per SLO excerpts) | Source |
+|---|---|---|
+| VMBO | Listening **A2**, speaking/conversation **A2**, writing **A1**, reading **A2/B1** ("haalbaar geacht") | [SLO: ERK streefniveaus Engels](https://www.slo.nl/handreikingen/vmbo/handreiking-se-engels-vmbo/examenprogramma/erk-streefniveaus/) |
+| VMBO-bb / kb / gt, speaking | A2 target; attained roughly A1 (bb), A2 (kb), A2/B1 (gt) | [SLO: eindniveau gespreksvaardigheid](https://www.slo.nl/publish/pages/3186/eindniveau-gespreksvaardigheid-engels-in-het-voortgezet-onderwijs.pdf) |
+| HAVO | Speaking **B1+**, listening **B1**, writing **B1**; reading **B2\*** (asterisk unexplained in the excerpt) | [SLO overview](https://www.slo.nl/thema/vakspecifieke-thema/mvt/erk/leraar-vo/niveaus-vo/niveaus-havo-vwo-du-fa-sp/), [SLO writing study](https://slo.nl/publish/pages/2769/erk-niveau-schrijfvaardigheid-engels-duits-en-frans.pdf) |
+| VWO | Speaking **B2**, listening **B2**, writing **B2**; reading **C1** "bij een ruime voldoende" (Cito 2013 standard-setting) | same |
+
+Other points:
+- The 2007 exam programme links havo and vwo to the CEFR, but exam items sit around B2 for vwo and just below B2 for havo ([SLO handreiking schoolexamen](https://www.slo.nl/publish/pages/3038/handreiking-schoolexamen-mvt-duits-engels-frans-havo-vwo.pdf)).
+- **The exam programmes are being renewed.** Definitive draft programmes exist for [havo](https://www.slo.nl/publish/pages/22912/definitief-conceptexamenprogramma-engelse-taal-en-cultuur-havo.pdf), [vwo](https://www.slo.nl/publish/pages/22913/definitief-conceptexamenprogramma-engelse-taal-en-cultuur-vwo.pdf) and [vmbo GL/TL](https://www.slo.nl/publish/pages/22911/definitief-conceptexamenprogramma-engelse-taal-en-cultuur-vmbo-gltl.pdf), each with a CEFR section. An explanatory document was reportedly planned for November 2026, so the official numbers may change.
+- **Per-year (jaar 1–3) targets:** no official per-year CEFR table was found. SLO has "tussendoelen" advice for the lower years ([SLO advies tussendoelen](https://www.slo.nl/publish/pages/3940/advies-tussendoelen-kernvakken-onderbouw-vo.pdf)), and a test provider's table lists onderbouw levels (A2 havo, A2/B1 vwo, A1/A2 vmbo) without clear skill headings ([AMN productinformatie](https://amn.nl/onderwijs/taal-en-rekentoetsen/productinformatie-engels.pdf)). Cambridge's school pages are commercial, not official.
+
+**Comparison with the app's table** (`src/data/cefrTrackYearTargets.ts`, described there as "the school's curriculum benchmark table"):
+
+| Cell in the app | App says | Official end-point per excerpts | Observation |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| jaar-4 VMBO-tl | B1–B2 | A2 target, A2/B1 attained | App looks **higher** |
+| jaar-4 VMBO-bb / kb | A2–B1 | A2 (writing A1) | App's top end is higher |
+| jaar-5 HAVO | B2 | B1 / B1+ (reading B2) | App looks higher except reading |
+| jaar-6 VWO | B2–C1 | B2 (reading C1) | Plausible as a range |
+
+**Suggested next steps:** (1) open the SLO documents above and confirm the figures; (2) decide whether the app should show **per-skill** targets (the official numbers differ by skill, the app has one range); (3) record the source of every cell in the data file; (4) treat the jaar 1–3 cells as the school's own estimates, and say so in the UI.
